        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T13:31:05Z",
          "note": "model-registry.ts internally calls readModels() inside writeModels() to build the 'existing models' set for deletion detection. This incurs a second filesystem read on every write. A future optimization could accept an optional `previousModels` parameter to allow callers that already hold the registry in memory to skip the re-read. For the current usage pattern (API handler reads then writes in the same request) this is negligible but worth noting."
